1
00:00:03,334 --> 00:00:07,433
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:16,167
[gagging, gasping]

3
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:18,470
Had bad nachos again...

4
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:22,499
Have to tell everyone...there's bad nachos...

5
00:00:22,499 --> 00:00:25,600
[coughing, gagging]

6
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,633
Aaagh...

7
00:00:26,633 --> 00:00:27,167
REBEL: You're here!

8
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:27,767
[gagging]

9
00:00:27,767 --> 00:00:28,700
WOMAN: Dr. Freeman?

10
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:29,900
Don't move. I'll kill you.

11
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,067
WOMAN: Gordon Freeman? Is that you?

12
00:00:32,067 --> 00:00:32,567
What?

13
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:33,867
WOMAN: You've made it here this quickly?

14
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:36,767
WOMAN: Well, Eli is going to be
amazed--not to mention relieved.

15
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:38,700
There's not enough blood going to my head.

16
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:40,800
MOSSMAN: I'm Dr. Mossman, Dr. Judith Mossman.

17
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:41,601
Feels bad.

18
00:00:41,601 --> 00:00:43,967
MOSSMAN: I've been hearing about you
since long before the Black Mesa incident.

19
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:44,900
Don't black out...

20
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,300
MOSSMAN: Ah, Black Mesa!

21
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:47,133
Don't black out!

22
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:48,133
MOSSMAN: I do so envy you...

23
00:00:48,133 --> 00:00:49,433
Nnnghhhhh!

24
00:00:49,433 --> 00:00:51,367
MOSSMAN: ...Dr. Kleiner when they
were at the top of their field.

25
00:00:51,367 --> 00:00:52,600
Kleiner! Right!

26
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,167
REBEL: Here's where we turn
it all around, eh, Freeman?

27
00:00:54,167 --> 00:00:56,600
Did he get you, too?! He's an animal!

28
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,433
[coughing]

29
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:59,400
MOSSMAN: I'll take you down
to Eli right away.

30
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,300
MOSSMAN: He would never forgive me...

31
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,400
So, did YOU gas me or was it her?

32
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,367
Answer me!

33
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:05,733
Never mind. It's actually not a bad idea,

34
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:07,867
and wouldn't have mattered
if I had my helmet.

35
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:10,000
So, once again, all roads lead to Kleiner.

36
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,233
MOSSMAN: We could certainly
use the extra help around here.

37
00:01:12,233 --> 00:01:13,167
[growling]

38
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:15,000
MOSSMAN: We've covered a lot of
ground in the last few months,

39
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,900
MOSSMAN: but things would go so much faster
if we had more people with your training.

40
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,467
Yeah, that's kind of true
of everything these days.

41
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:22,967
MOSSMAN: We're closing in on a
reliable local teleport technology...

42
00:01:22,967 --> 00:01:24,535
Oh, they KNEW it was unreliable.

43
00:01:24,535 --> 00:01:26,033
MOSSMAN: ...something the
Combine still hasn't mastered.

44
00:01:26,033 --> 00:01:26,767
They knew.

45
00:01:26,767 --> 00:01:28,833
MOSSMAN: Eli thinks their
portals are string-based...

46
00:01:28,833 --> 00:01:29,633
He's wrong.

47
00:01:29,633 --> 00:01:31,167
MOSSMAN: ...similar to our Calabi-Yau model,

48
00:01:31,167 --> 00:01:33,700
MOSSMAN: but they've failed to
factor in the dark energy equations.

49
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:34,800
Oh, you're one of THOSE.

50
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,633
MOSSMAN: They can tunnel through from
their universe, but once they're here...

51
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:37,266
"Universe"?

52
00:01:37,266 --> 00:01:38,633
MOSSMAN: ...they're dependent
on local transportation.

53
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:40,900
MOSSMAN: If they know what
we're doing with entanglement...

54
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:43,067
Wait, it's a separate universe?

55
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:44,833
I'm going to have to see your math.

56
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:48,767
MOSSMAN: [laughs] Listen to
me. I sound like a post-doc.

57
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:50,000
Is this the only entrance?

58
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,167
MOSSMAN: I'm just so excited to think

59
00:01:51,167 --> 00:01:53,467
MOSSMAN: that we'll finally
have a chance to work together.

60
00:01:53,467 --> 00:01:57,367
Y'know, that's a real nice thought, but I
was followed. I don't think we're secure.

61
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:01,600
MOSSMAN: Oh yes. Dr. Kleiner compressed
the Xen Relay far beyond anything

62
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,267
Fuck...
MOSSMAN: he imagined at Black Mesa.

63
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:06,051
MOSSMAN: We've figured out how to
use Xen as an unexpressed axis--

64
00:02:06,051 --> 00:02:06,752
OH!

65
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:08,233
MOSSMAN: --effectively a
dimensional slingshot...

66
00:02:08,233 --> 00:02:10,022
There goes MY appetite!

67
00:02:10,022 --> 00:02:12,367
MOSSMAN: ...come back in local space
without having to pass through.

68
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:15,024
What?! Are they serious?!

69
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:17,667
MOSSMAN: Oh! Here's Eli now.

70
00:02:17,667 --> 00:02:20,300
Should I ask which one's Eli?

71
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:22,072
This is a nuthouse!

72
00:02:22,072 --> 00:02:23,833
MOSSMAN: Eli! Look who
I found in the airlock.

73
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:25,300
It smells like sex in here.

74
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:27,296
ELI: Gordon Freeman! Heh.

75
00:02:27,296 --> 00:02:27,754
ELI: Let me get a look at you, man.

76
00:02:27,754 --> 00:02:31,254
Whoa, yeah. I definitely don't know you.
ELI: Let me get a look at you, man.

77
00:02:31,254 --> 00:02:33,633
I would've remembered that leg.

78
00:02:33,633 --> 00:02:35,570
ELI: Now let's see. The last time I saw you,

79
00:02:35,570 --> 00:02:39,267
ELI: I sent you up for help
after the resonance cascade.

80
00:02:39,267 --> 00:02:42,233
ELI: Heh, I never thought it would
take you this long to get back to me.

81
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:43,363
A lot of people died.

82
00:02:43,363 --> 00:02:44,556
ELI: Welcome to the lab, anyway.

83
00:02:44,556 --> 00:02:47,968
ELI: It's not Black Mesa, but
it's served us well enough.

84
00:02:47,968 --> 00:02:51,031
MOSSMAN: It's going to be a lot more
like Black Mesa with Gordon here to help.

85
00:02:51,031 --> 00:02:51,607
Well...

86
00:02:51,607 --> 00:02:55,630
ELI: Right you are. MIT graduates
are few and far between these days.

87
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:56,534
Recognize!

88
00:02:56,534 --> 00:02:58,063
ELI: We'll get you out of that hazard suit

89
00:02:58,063 --> 00:03:01,056
ELI: and back into your
labcoat where you belong.

90
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:04,233
MOSSMAN: Let me just finish up some
work, and I'll see what I can dig up.

91
00:03:04,233 --> 00:03:05,333
MOSSMAN: Dr. Freeman?

92
00:03:05,333 --> 00:03:05,880
What?

93
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:09,433
MOSSMAN: It's been a real honor. I'm
looking forward to working together.

94
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:12,100
Well, I WOULD be except that we have--

95
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:13,300
ELI: Feel free to take a look around.

96
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:16,141
Yeah, listen. I was trying
to tell her I was followed.

97
00:03:16,141 --> 00:03:18,002
Do you know if there's a w...

98
00:03:18,002 --> 00:03:21,033
Okay, you're too old for
this. Who's in charge?

99
00:03:21,033 --> 00:03:23,833
If you tell me it's the
alien, I'm leaving right now.

100
00:03:23,833 --> 00:03:25,800
God, is this even real?

101
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:28,593
This is too nice! This isn't going to last!

102
00:03:28,593 --> 00:03:32,333
You can't play with my emotions
like this! I won't let them!

103
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:33,933
MOSSMAN: Oh, Dr. Freeman.
You should stay with Eli.

104
00:03:33,933 --> 00:03:34,522
Oh.

105
00:03:34,522 --> 00:03:35,100
MOSSMAN: Go on. I'll be with you shortly.

106
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,467
This is good.
MOSSMAN: Go on. I'll be with you shortly.

107
00:03:36,467 --> 00:03:38,167
Okay, that's good you're
watching the kitchen,

108
00:03:38,167 --> 00:03:40,100
but honestly, that's not enough.

109
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:41,533
We'll talk about that later.

110
00:03:41,533 --> 00:03:45,200
Do you have a view of the exterior?
These look like they're somewhere else.

111
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:49,133
I mean if we see them coming, then
seconds matter. You know what I'm saying?

112
00:03:49,133 --> 00:03:50,267
Dammit. Is that it?

113
00:03:50,267 --> 00:03:51,133
MOSSMAN: Dr. Freeman?

114
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:51,533
What?!

115
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:54,667
MOSSMAN: I figured you and Eli would want
to talk about old times. We can talk later.

116
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:56,600
I don't know Eli.

117
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:00,733
Doesn't matter. You know how to use
the cameras. Watch the exterior.

118
00:04:00,733 --> 00:04:03,267
Fuck! You're not even watching the outside.

119
00:04:03,267 --> 00:04:07,367
ELI: Fine scientist, Judith. She
was up for your job at Black Mesa,

120
00:04:07,367 --> 00:04:10,167
ELI: but you edged her out
with your Innsbruck experience.

121
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:12,133
Oh, I'm sure it was more than that.

122
00:04:12,133 --> 00:04:15,333
Little Miss Dark Energy
hasn't impressed me so far.

123
00:04:15,333 --> 00:04:18,333
Jesus Christ, I forgot about you.

124
00:04:18,333 --> 00:04:20,371
Do I even want to know what you're doing?

125
00:04:20,371 --> 00:04:22,333
Looks like monitoring software.

126
00:04:22,333 --> 00:04:24,367
Or maybe he just hit the boss key.

127
00:04:24,367 --> 00:04:27,591
No, don't look at me.
I'll deal with you later.

128
00:04:27,591 --> 00:04:29,500
What the hell is this?

129
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:31,767
Is it one of their eggs?

130
00:04:31,767 --> 00:04:33,081
It probably is.

131
00:04:33,081 --> 00:04:36,400
There's going to be some changes
around here if we survive the night.

132
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,533
Okay, think, think.

133
00:04:38,533 --> 00:04:42,200
The zappers aren't going to kill
me immediately. That's something.

134
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:45,433
"Earth Surrenders". Yeah, this
would've been useful earlier.

135
00:04:45,433 --> 00:04:47,033
I can't focus...

136
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:51,800
The zappers are submissive now. They might
poison my food or kill me in my sleep,

137
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,400
but either way, I have time.

138
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:55,500
The troops will discover this place soon,

139
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:59,167
but if they sound a scout and we kill
'em, that might buy me half an hour.

140
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:03,167
Jesus, I can't even read this. I'm
going to need a new prescription.

141
00:05:03,167 --> 00:05:05,433
That's another not-today problem.

142
00:05:06,419 --> 00:05:07,167
ALYX: Oh, Gordon!

143
00:05:07,167 --> 00:05:08,300
Oh my fucking god...

144
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:09,633
ALYX: The vortigaunts said you were here!

145
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:12,133
ALYX: I can't believe you
made it so quickly on foot.

146
00:05:12,133 --> 00:05:14,800
Yeah, a LOT of people are
confused I'm still alive.

147
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:18,700
ALYX: Huh, he earned it. I guess you
proved you can handle yourself out there.

148
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:19,467
What's wrong you?

149
00:05:19,467 --> 00:05:22,133
ELI: There's nothing Gordon can't handle.

150
00:05:22,133 --> 00:05:24,433
ELI: With the possible exception of you.

151
00:05:24,433 --> 00:05:25,767
That is very true.

152
00:05:25,767 --> 00:05:26,900
ELI: Hahhhhh...

153
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:29,667
I don't blame the old man
for trying to pawn her off.

154
00:05:29,667 --> 00:05:32,733
That's the same principle
behind hand grenades also.

155
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:35,467
God dammit! Why is everyone here so casual?!

156
00:05:35,467 --> 00:05:37,667
It's like everyone is in denial.

157
00:05:37,667 --> 00:05:39,800
This is the Lab of the Lotus-Eaters.

158
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,133
ELI: Take a look at this, Gordon.

159
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,667
[sighs]

160
00:05:42,667 --> 00:05:44,633
Fine. What is it?

161
00:05:45,818 --> 00:05:48,933
Oh god! I remember that!

162
00:05:48,933 --> 00:05:51,500
You're trying to break my mind, old man?

163
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,167
Well, congratulations. You got my attention.

164
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:57,567
I think we should turn this off. How do
we know this isn't some sort of beacon?

165
00:05:57,567 --> 00:06:01,767
Y'know, I never learned what went wrong
with the experiment; this is so dangerous!

166
00:06:01,767 --> 00:06:03,800
Hey! How do you turn this off?!

167
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:06,300
Maybe this is his way of
getting me to shut up.

168
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:09,700
"Gordon, all you've done is
complain since you got here.

169
00:06:10,967 --> 00:06:15,633
"How about I teleport your
ass back to alien hell?

170
00:06:15,633 --> 00:06:19,033
"Bet you'd stop criticizing my lab, then."

171
00:06:19,033 --> 00:06:21,900
All right, so I don't
really have any allies here.

172
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:24,067
I'm more like a zoo exhibit to them.

173
00:06:24,067 --> 00:06:26,267
"Ooh! Look at the Freeman!"

174
00:06:26,267 --> 00:06:27,900
Well, they're going to die.

175
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:30,467
MOSSMAN: Alyx, I thought you were on watch.

176
00:06:30,467 --> 00:06:32,567
ALYX: The vortigaunts relieved
me so I could come see Gordon.

177
00:06:32,567 --> 00:06:32,900
What?

178
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,867
ALYX: Anyway, I should be in
here working on the portal.

179
00:06:34,867 --> 00:06:35,667
The aliens?

180
00:06:35,667 --> 00:06:36,900
MOSSMAN: I have the repairs well in hand.

181
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:37,867
That's what you call the aliens?

182
00:06:37,867 --> 00:06:40,233
MOSSMAN: Someone misjudged the
capacity of the Combine thyristor.

183
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,633
The vertigos?

184
00:06:41,633 --> 00:06:42,867
ALYX: Are you blaming me?

185
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:43,467
Dammit.

186
00:06:43,467 --> 00:06:43,914
MOSSMAN: No!

187
00:06:43,914 --> 00:06:44,646
Not now!

188
00:06:44,646 --> 00:06:46,800
MOSSMAN: Not at all. It was a calculation
error, not a mechanical problem.

189
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,400
You're not listening.

190
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:50,667
ALYX: Then maybe you should let
me do the calculations next time,

191
00:06:50,667 --> 00:06:52,133
ALYX: as well as installing it.

192
00:06:52,133 --> 00:06:53,167
MOSSMAN: Alyx, really...

193
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:54,173
Drama! Great...

194
00:06:54,173 --> 00:06:56,633
MOSSMAN: Sometimes I think you
deliberately misunderstand me.

195
00:06:56,633 --> 00:07:00,067
ELI: Ahem. Alyx, why don't
you take Gordon along

196
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,733
ELI: and give him some
practice with the gravity gun?

197
00:07:02,733 --> 00:07:03,133
Wait...!

198
00:07:03,133 --> 00:07:06,267
ALYX: Sure... Come on, Gordon.
Let's go have some fun.

199
00:07:06,267 --> 00:07:06,667
No..!

200
00:07:06,667 --> 00:07:10,267
MOSSMAN: The Zero Point Energy Field
Manipulator is not a toy, Alyx!

201
00:07:10,267 --> 00:07:12,033
ALYX: Ugh. Let's get out of here.

202
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:16,500
Yes! Showing me the exits is probably the
best thing any of you can do at this point.

203
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,967
You're all too far gone.

204
00:07:17,967 --> 00:07:19,800
One more time: I was followed;

205
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:22,133
this place is impressive,
but it's not NORAD;

206
00:07:22,133 --> 00:07:23,433
they're going to find it, and kill you.

207
00:07:23,433 --> 00:07:24,133
Bye.

208
00:07:24,133 --> 00:07:26,767
And you! Do you even
understand what you did to me?

209
00:07:26,767 --> 00:07:28,567
ALYX: So, I see you've met Dr. Mossman.

210
00:07:28,567 --> 00:07:29,933
I guess not!

211
00:07:29,933 --> 00:07:32,967
ALYX: She's one of the main reasons
I spend so much time outside.

212
00:07:32,967 --> 00:07:34,400
ALYX: You should hear her drone on

213
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:37,867
ALYX: about how it should have been her
in the Black Mesa Test Chamber that day.

214
00:07:37,867 --> 00:07:39,500
Oh, she said that?!

215
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,633
ALYX: I'm sorry. I shouldn't
be talking behind her back.

216
00:07:41,633 --> 00:07:44,233
ALYX: It just gets a bit
claustrophobic down here.

217
00:07:44,233 --> 00:07:46,600
Okay, so she's worse than I thought.

218
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,933
My god, it's the Ship of Fools down here.

219
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:51,167
ALYX: That's the old passage to Ravenholm.

220
00:07:51,167 --> 00:07:52,033
What's that?

221
00:07:52,033 --> 00:07:53,267
ALYX: We don't go there anymore...

222
00:07:53,267 --> 00:07:56,100
But that IS an exit?
I can open it from here?

223
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:58,927
Okay, good, good. Keep
showing me stuff like this.

224
00:07:58,927 --> 00:07:59,667
ALYX: Come on.

225
00:07:59,667 --> 00:08:01,033
Oh, this is another one?

226
00:08:01,033 --> 00:08:04,400
That's good. They probably won't come
from both sides without us noticing.

227
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:07,767
Though who knows? You left guard
duty to the vertigos, right?

228
00:08:07,767 --> 00:08:10,933
They're probably out there
right now waving signal flares.

229
00:08:10,933 --> 00:08:12,600
Okay, so do you want me to gas you?

230
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,567
I don't know what button to press.

231
00:08:15,567 --> 00:08:17,833
God, I feel like I'm in the Twilight Zone,

232
00:08:17,833 --> 00:08:20,867
and the twist isn't that the
Earth has been invaded by aliens.

233
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:23,333
It's that everyone left
is acting like an alien!

234
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:25,267
Everyone is acting WAY too calm!

235
00:08:25,267 --> 00:08:28,867
It's not even optimism. It's just
a complete divorce from reality!

236
00:08:28,867 --> 00:08:31,433
ALYX: So, here we are. The scrapyard.

237
00:08:31,433 --> 00:08:33,567
That includes you, by the way.

238
00:08:33,567 --> 00:08:34,524
Well...

239
00:08:35,533 --> 00:08:38,867
I don't like this canyon at
all. It feels like a killbox.

240
00:08:38,867 --> 00:08:41,000
ALYX: This is the gravity gun
my father was talking about.

241
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,433
At least it's quiet.

242
00:08:42,433 --> 00:08:46,533
ALYX: You can call it the 'Zero Point Energy
Field Manipulator' if you really want to.

243
00:08:46,533 --> 00:08:47,333
What?

244
00:08:47,333 --> 00:08:50,267
ALYX: It's designed for
handling hazardous materials,

245
00:08:50,267 --> 00:08:52,428
ALYX: but we mainly use it for heavy lifting.

246
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,500
ALYX: Give it a try.

247
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:57,519
Okay?  Why are...?

248
00:08:57,519 --> 00:09:01,933
ALYX: The primary trigger emits a charge.
You can punt stuff and send it flying.

249
00:09:01,933 --> 00:09:02,967
I missed something.

250
00:09:02,967 --> 00:09:05,333
ALYX: I've found it handy
for clearing minefields.

251
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:07,033
Oh, it's for mines?

252
00:09:07,033 --> 00:09:08,767
I have--WHUGH!

253
00:09:08,767 --> 00:09:11,533
OH! That woke me up...

254
00:09:11,533 --> 00:09:13,700
You sure I'm pointing this the right way?

255
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:15,533
ALYX: The secondary trigger
lets you grab things.

256
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:16,100
Oh...

257
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,533
ALYX: You can throw them with the primary.

258
00:09:17,533 --> 00:09:18,767
Oh my god.

259
00:09:18,767 --> 00:09:20,500
ALYX: Once you've picked something
up you can drop it gently--

260
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:20,967
Ah?!

261
00:09:20,967 --> 00:09:22,833
ALYX: --by pressing your
secondary trigger again.

262
00:09:22,833 --> 00:09:24,100
This is incredible!

263
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:25,466
ALYX: Pick up some stuff and toss it.

264
00:09:27,533 --> 00:09:28,633
Okay, project...

265
00:09:28,633 --> 00:09:29,833
[quickly exhaling]

266
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:30,900
UGH!

267
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:31,800
[coughs]

268
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:35,367
It feels like Jesus
shoving me out of heaven!

269
00:09:35,367 --> 00:09:38,933
This changes gravity? There's
so many applications for this!

270
00:09:38,933 --> 00:09:41,026
ALYX: You can also pull
stuff over from a distance.

271
00:09:41,026 --> 00:09:42,933
Transportation, defense...

272
00:09:42,933 --> 00:09:45,000
ALYX: Try grabbing those barrels
from that ledge up there.

273
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,633
That's a fair range.

274
00:09:46,633 --> 00:09:49,800
What kind of battery does this
have? How long is the charge?

275
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:50,533
Huh-HOH!

276
00:09:50,533 --> 00:09:51,800
ALYX: All right.

277
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:55,120
And now I want to press the
OTHER button, not the trigger.

278
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:55,933
Yeah.

279
00:09:55,933 --> 00:09:57,533
This is astounding.

280
00:09:57,533 --> 00:10:00,300
And all they're doing is
using this to move boxes?

281
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:02,467
ALYX: See if you can stack
some stuff to climb up here.

282
00:10:02,467 --> 00:10:04,733
This is just a game for her, isn't it?

283
00:10:04,733 --> 00:10:07,000
She has no contextual awareness.

284
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,400
I think she might have the mind of a child.

285
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,378
Okay, well...

286
00:10:11,378 --> 00:10:15,000
I'll play along for now. I
need to see the exit anyway.

287
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,067
ALYX: Try stacking some things.

288
00:10:17,067 --> 00:10:19,333
ALYX: Grab something with
your secondary trigger,

289
00:10:19,333 --> 00:10:21,633
ALYX: then press the same
trigger again to drop it gently.

290
00:10:21,633 --> 00:10:22,233
Yeah...

291
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:23,500
ALYX: All right.

292
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:27,167
She has to make sure she tells me
the rules--makes her feel important.

293
00:10:27,167 --> 00:10:29,600
Yeah, look at her run. She's just a kid.

294
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,867
I don't even know if
I can be mad at her now.

295
00:10:31,867 --> 00:10:34,233
This is all just a game of
Cops and Robbers to her.

296
00:10:35,033 --> 00:10:38,533
Okay, we're in the future, so I
guess she grew up during this mess?

297
00:10:38,533 --> 00:10:40,500
It must have stunted her development.

298
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,567
ALYX: Now let me call Dog.
He loves to play fetch.

299
00:10:42,567 --> 00:10:44,033
Yeah, she's showing me her dog.

300
00:10:44,033 --> 00:10:46,929
Christ, we gotta speed this up.
ALYX: Dog! Come!

301
00:10:47,433 --> 00:10:48,167
What the fuck?

302
00:10:48,933 --> 00:10:52,576
Hey, that's not a dog. Don't
know if you understand that.

303
00:10:52,576 --> 00:10:54,300
Oh my god. We have a mech.

304
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:56,000
It's pretty mobile, too.

305
00:10:56,733 --> 00:10:58,233
There's a lot of tech in this.

306
00:10:58,233 --> 00:11:00,033
ALYX: Good doggie.

307
00:11:00,033 --> 00:11:01,633
ALYX: Gordon, this is Dog.

308
00:11:01,633 --> 00:11:04,200
ALYX: My dad built him to
protect me when I was a kid.

309
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:07,033
ALYX: First model was about yay-high.

310
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:09,267
Why isn't THIS on guard duty?

311
00:11:09,267 --> 00:11:10,433
ALYX: Haven't I, boy?

312
00:11:11,533 --> 00:11:13,267
ALYX: Okay, Dog,
let's play catch with Gordon.

313
00:11:13,267 --> 00:11:14,500
Oh my god.

314
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,600
ALYX: You'll need to use the gravity gun.

315
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,433
This is such a long day.

316
00:11:17,433 --> 00:11:18,900
ALYX: Go ahead, Dog! Throw!

317
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:21,833
Listen, I really am interested
in the engineering here,

318
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:23,833
but this isn't a good time for that.

319
00:11:23,833 --> 00:11:26,533
I mean, we've clearly had a
battery breakthrough somewhere,

320
00:11:26,533 --> 00:11:30,033
and this AI seems pretty good,
though I'd have to test it.

321
00:11:30,733 --> 00:11:32,509
Yeah, see, now I'm getting distracted.

322
00:11:32,509 --> 00:11:33,200
ALYX: Throw another, Dog.

323
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:35,400
No, we don't have time for this shit.

324
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:38,600
I'm not seeing an exit. Is
this just some giant sinkhole?

325
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:40,123
We need to kill these lights.

326
00:11:41,433 --> 00:11:42,133
All right...

327
00:11:42,133 --> 00:11:42,933
ALYX: Another one, Dog.

328
00:11:42,933 --> 00:11:45,633
Why don't we play with Dog later,

329
00:11:45,633 --> 00:11:49,933
because Uncle Gordon has some grown-up
things he needs to take care of?

330
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:52,081
Okay?

331
00:11:52,081 --> 00:11:53,267
ALYX: Go ahead, Dog! Throw!

332
00:11:53,267 --> 00:11:54,933
Well, it was worth a shot.

333
00:11:54,933 --> 00:11:58,800
I don't want to make her cry,
but this is going nowhere fast.

334
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,233
We're lit up like a runway here.

335
00:12:00,233 --> 00:12:01,167
ALYX: No, Dog!

336
00:12:01,167 --> 00:12:03,700
Oh, damn, that's a lot of power!

337
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:06,967
And it looks like the AI isn't
much better than what we had.

338
00:12:06,967 --> 00:12:08,800
[close explosion]

339
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:10,578
Whoa! I felt that!

340
00:12:10,578 --> 00:12:11,933
[whistling sound]

341
00:12:11,933 --> 00:12:12,470
[explosion]

342
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:15,587
OH NO! I WAS RIGHT! I WAS RIGHT AGAIN!

343
00:12:15,587 --> 00:12:18,947
WHY AM I CURSED TO ALWAYS
BE RIGHT ABOUT EVERYTHING?!

344
00:12:18,947 --> 00:12:21,191
I'M LIKE A MODERN GREEK TRAGEDY!

345
00:12:21,191 --> 00:12:23,049
THEY'LL WRITE POEMS ABOUT ME!

346
00:12:23,049 --> 00:12:25,433
[machine gun fire]
OH NO! NOT THE CHOPPER! NOT AGAIN!

347
00:12:25,433 --> 00:12:27,267
I CAN'T TAKE IT! STOP IT!

348
00:12:27,267 --> 00:12:29,233
Shut the door! Shut the door!
Go go go go GO!

349
00:12:30,037 --> 00:12:33,992
C'MON, YOU FUCKING AI! IT'S
A BARREL, NOT A PERSON!

350
00:12:33,992 --> 00:12:35,700
ALYX: This is Alyx, do you read?!

351
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:37,033
ELI: Alyx! Honey!

352
00:12:37,033 --> 00:12:38,333
OPEN THE DOOR!

353
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:39,367
ELI: Where are you, Alyx?!

354
00:12:39,367 --> 00:12:42,300
ALYX: We're in the scrapyard
airlock stuck in a full autocycle.

355
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:43,967
OPEN THE FUCKING DOOR!

356
00:12:43,967 --> 00:12:44,867
ALYX: He's right here.

357
00:12:44,867 --> 00:12:46,767
ELI: Good. I want you two to--

358
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:49,600
ALYX: Dad?!
You've gotta be kidding me...

359
00:12:50,033 --> 00:12:52,033
ELI: Take Gordon out of
here! Head for the coast!

360
00:12:52,033 --> 00:12:54,267
OPEN THE DOOR!
ELI: Do not go through Rav--

361
00:12:54,267 --> 00:12:57,967
"Oh, wh-what was I saying?
Let me go find my glasses."

362
00:12:57,967 --> 00:12:59,600
Your dad just killed us!

363
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,600
Yeah, just beat this thing
down. It's all we can do.

364
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,533
ALYX: Get it open!

365
00:13:05,533 --> 00:13:08,167
I want to see some Three
Laws of Robotics rage.

366
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:13,918
Ohhhh, you got us into this mess and
you're going to get us out of it.

367
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:14,667
ALYX: Come on!

368
00:13:14,667 --> 00:13:17,733
Y'know, I'm having a really
hard time staying positive!

369
00:13:17,733 --> 00:13:20,233
If you told me you had a
secret submarine base here,

370
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:21,600
I think that would cheer me up.

371
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:25,936
[loud explosion]
OHH! AAH, MY LEG! MY LEG!

372
00:13:25,936 --> 00:13:27,533
Aahhh...!

373
00:13:27,533 --> 00:13:29,000
ALYX: Gordon, you need to get out of here!

374
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,100
Shit potatoes...

375
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,100
ALYX: I can't leave my father.

376
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,000
Aaah...

377
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,367
ALYX: Dog, take Gordon
to the Ravenholm tunnel,

378
00:13:34,367 --> 00:13:37,700
ALYX: then circle around and
try to meet up with me. Hurry!

379
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:40,000
I could squeeze through that,
but y'know what?

380
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,467
Getting away from you is fine by me.

381
00:13:42,467 --> 00:13:45,367
Can the AI actually understand all that?

382
00:13:45,367 --> 00:13:47,367
Seems to. Wow.

383
00:13:47,367 --> 00:13:49,467
Maybe it's working off of buzzwords.

384
00:13:49,467 --> 00:13:51,800
I mean, AI is good until it's not.

385
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:54,267
Oh, radiation! Yeah, that's great.

386
00:13:54,267 --> 00:13:58,533
Why is there so much radioactive material
in a hydroelectric plant, anyway?

387
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:03,533
Oh, damn, I should've checked to see if
it takes my voice commands or just hers.

388
00:14:03,533 --> 00:14:05,600
That would've been a
nice going-away present.

389
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:08,400
Of course, that means it would
take enemy voice commands also,

390
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:12,067
but the odds they would be smart enough
to figure that out are basically zero.

391
00:14:12,633 --> 00:14:16,567
But then they could say something like
"Flank left", and that could be a problem.

392
00:14:16,567 --> 00:14:19,033
Yeah, I think it's a
bluff; there's no ticking.

393
00:14:19,033 --> 00:14:20,300
What a day...

394
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:24,533
Y'know, I'm actually less nervous
now that the other shoe dropped.

395
00:14:24,533 --> 00:14:26,933
WHOA! That solved THAT problem!

396
00:14:26,933 --> 00:14:29,600
It's never too late to get shot, huh?

397
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:30,333
It's just...

398
00:14:32,767 --> 00:14:35,000
Oh, okay. Maybe this is the equivalent

399
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,333
of those prop security cams that
are just there to scare burglars.

400
00:14:38,333 --> 00:14:42,167
Or maybe this is backdoor surveillance, and
this place was infiltrated the whole time.

401
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:43,767
But am I being recorded?

402
00:14:44,233 --> 00:14:49,867
OH! SHIT! I DO NOT GET A MINUTE,
DO I?! I DO NOT GET ONE MINUTE!

403
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:54,267
It just... It just heard me and
rolled the dice, hoping to land on me.

404
00:14:54,267 --> 00:14:55,036
Fu...

405
00:14:56,167 --> 00:14:58,855
This is going to be a
long night too, isn't it?

406
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:06,700
I should've just asked her to let me
ride the robot like a horse out of here.

407
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:10,618
She would think it's funny and
I would leave. Everybody wins.

